.TH CCOL_CHAN_SEND_ZC 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
ccol_chan_send_zc \- send a message through the ccol_channel (it blocks)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cthreadcomm.h>

ccol_retval_t ccol_chan_send_zc(ccol_channel *ch, c_message_t *msg);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
The function picks the correct queue itself, from the thread that
calls it:
- The owner thread sends to the ccol_owner_to_workers queue
- A worker thread sends to the ccol_workers_to_owner queue

The function blocks until the queue has free space and then transfers
the ownership.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
ch   Channel to send through
msg  Message to send. On success the ownership of the data moves to the
     channel.
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
ccol_success       - The function sent the message
ccol_invalid_args  - ch or msg is NULL, or the check of msg fails
ccol_not_permitted - Sends on the chosen direction are turned off
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The function blocks until the chosen queue has free space.
The function picks the direction itself from the ID of the thread.
On failure, the caller keeps the ownership of msg->data.
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ccol_chan_try_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_timed_send_zc (3),
.BR ccol_chan_recv_zc (3)
